#baloni problem-:
//TEACH HOW TO SEARCH/MARK ELEMENT FAST USING VALUE BASED INDEXING IN ARRAY/BOOL
greedy (chain/Simulation)+reuse resources:
```
const ll max= 1000000;
vector<bool> err(max,0);
int arrows=0;
for(int j=0; j<n;j++){
    int y= arr[j];
if(1==err[y]){
    err[y]=0;
}
else{
    arrows++;
}
err[y-1]=1;
}```

#A Classic doubly linked list problem-;
Uva armies buddies-;
Neighbor Tracking+ Dynamic Deletion+ Implicit Linked List
it have bunch of solution -;
the easiest one is using set and taking lowerbound and upperbound-1 and delete element between it O(log n) 
but using double linked list it costs O(1) per deletion 
BEST WAY FOR tracking is FENWICK TREE AND USING DSU (WILL TALK LATER IN DEEP)

